course: dictionary
lesson: 11855
title: Compound words: bodied
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bodied is usually not alone. It joins another word with a hyphen, like able-bodied or full-bodied. Read the word in front first, because it tells you which kind of body is meant.
explain: «The able-bodied runners carried the water to the finish line.» Able-bodied means fit and healthy, so the runners were strong enough to carry heavy water. Try swapping in fit and healthy: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «This tea has a full-bodied flavour.» A full-bodied flavour is strong and rich, not weak or watery. «The slim-bodied insect hid under a leaf» tells you the insect has a thin body. Check the first word, then the meaning follows.
fact: Bodied is usually part of a compound word, joined to another word with a hyphen.
fact: «Able-bodied» means fit and healthy.
fact: «Full-bodied» means strong and rich, often used for flavours like tea, coffee or wine.
fact: «Slim-bodied» means having a thin body, as in «a slim-bodied insect».
fact: In slang, «got bodied» means badly beaten in a game or an argument.
exercise: «The able-bodied firefighter carried the child out of the smoke.» What does able-bodied mean? | Very tired and sleepy | *Fit and healthy | Afraid of fire | Able to sing well
exercise: «This coffee has a full-bodied flavour.» What does full-bodied mean here? | *Strong and rich | Cold and bitter | Sweet, like sugar | Thin and watery
exercise: «The slim-bodied insect hid under a leaf.» Copy the word that tells you what kind of body it has. | hid | leaf | insect | *slim-bodied
test: The coach said, «We got bodied in the first half.» What does got bodied mean? | Given a prize | Won easily by a big margin | Taken to hospital | *Badly beaten
test: Bodied is part of a compound like full-bodied. What two words make up full-bodied? | *full and body | fill and bod | fun and body | full and bottle
exam: Ellie says the -bodied part of a word like able-bodied tells you what? | How old someone is | The colour of the clothes | The time of day | *The kind of body
